# XSH posix_spawnattr_getsigdefault() and posix_spawnattr_setsigdefault()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Effects are shown by really spawning this program as a child image. The
# functions return the error number; errno is not used. SIGKILL and SIGSTOP
# are not put in sets.

assertion  XSH.posix_spawnattr_getsigdefault.001
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getsigdefault.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getsigdefault.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       posix_spawnattr_getsigdefault() on a newly initialised object returns 0
           and stores an empty signal set (the destination was filled
           first).
test       t/001-default.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawnattr_getsigdefault.002
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getsigdefault.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getsigdefault.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       posix_spawnattr_setsigdefault() with a set of SIGUSR1, SIGTERM and
           SIGRTMIN returns 0 and posix_spawnattr_getsigdefault()
           returns 0 and stores exactly that set; a second object keeps
           its own different set.
test       t/002-roundtrip.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawnattr_getsigdefault.003
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getsigdefault.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       A later posix_spawnattr_setsigdefault() replaces the set (an empty set
           after a non-empty one reads back empty), and the attribute is
           a copy: changing the caller's set variable after the call
           does not change what is read back.
test       t/003-replace-copy.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawnattr_getsigdefault.004
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getsigdefault.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/posix_spawn.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       With POSIX_SPAWN_SETSIGDEF set and SIGUSR1 in the spawn-sigdefault set,
           a child of a parent that ignores SIGUSR1 and SIGUSR2 has
           SIGUSR1 at its default action while SIGUSR2 stays ignored.
test       t/004-effect.c
